From 3a49561a658db5c8a520330bda44a3ee7861e52d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:51:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] Gold, not blue, for every control's state
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Settings colours get a new choice, Gold, and it is the default: the
window as it always was, with a gold accent for its switches, ticks,
sliders, buttons and selected section. Plugins take that accent (the
kept plugin theme moves to a new key, so a blue one from before is not
used). In the meter's windows the Details switches, the History tabs and
links, a skill's active spec, focus rings and the scrollbar are gold, and
the update window's Notes button is grey. Meter Theme stays a choice.

The plugins' marks (dock tabs, Settings → Plugins) leave the blues out:
Mantra Watch's turns pink, this build's own plugins get icons of their
own, and a colour made from a plugin's id skips the blue range.
